@@ -11,9 +11,13 @@ of its booking desk, written in TypeScript with no runtime dependency.
 
 - Money is an integer number of euro cents; `total` is `dailyPrice` times the number of days; a rental of 3 days or more gets 10% off that
   full price, rounded to the nearest cent. `quote` and `book` both return the reduced total.
-- Times are ISO-8601 UTC strings with an explicit `Z`. A period starts and ends at midnight UTC and
+- Times are ISO-8601 UTC strings with an explicit `Z`. A daily period starts and ends at midnight UTC and
   `end` is the start of the day after the last rented day, so `2026-07-01T00:00:00Z` to
   `2026-07-02T00:00:00Z` is one day. Returned times are normalised to `toISOString()` form.
+- Hourly rental: `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice` (integer euro cents per hour). A period
+  shorter than a day that starts and ends on the hour costs `hourlyPrice` times the number of hours (no
+  discount); it may cross midnight. An item without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour. A period
+  of a day or more must still be whole UTC days. Overlap and `availability` rules are the same for hourly periods.
 - An item cannot be booked for overlapping periods; back-to-back periods are fine.
 - `availability({ start, end, kind? })` returns the sorted ids of the items, of that kind or of any kind when
   none is given, that are free for the whole period (same period rules as `quote`).
